<title>USA: Eltron, Zebra end merger talks.</title>
<headline>Eltron, Zebra end merger talks.</headline>
<dateline>SIMI VALLEY, Calif. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eltron International Inc and Zebra Technologies Corp Wednesday said they terminated merger discussions.</p>
<p>Donald Skinner, chairman and chief executive officer of Eltron and Edward Kaplan, chairman and chief executive officer of Zebra, said the companies have been unable to reach agreement on terms which would be mutually acceptable.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;We are disappointed,&quot; they said in a statement. &quot;However, this does not diminish our enthusiasm about the prospects our respective businesses face in the coming year.&quot;</p>
</text>
